  $ags_body$# SUBCONTRACTOR AGREEMENT

**AGS Decorating & Refurbishment Services Ltd**

## Schedule of Services

| Field | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Agreement dated | {{agreement_date}} |
| Agreement number | {{agreement_number}} |
| Client | AGS Decorating & Refurbishment Services Ltd of 1 Cabot House, Stocks Bridge Way, St. Ives, Cambridgeshire, PE27 5JL |
| Subcontractor | {{subcontractor_full_name}} of {{subcontractor_address}} |
| Commencement date | {{commencement_date}} |
| Expected completion date | {{expected_completion_date}} |
| Location of working | Various projects located around the Southeast of England. |
| Rate (excl. CIS deductions) | {{agreed_rate}} |
| Pay statement frequency | Twice monthly. A statement is issued alongside each payment |
| Pay frequency | Twice monthly, on the 15th and the last working day of each month. The payment on the 15th is for work completed between the 16th and the last calendar day of the previous month. The payment on the last working day of the month is for work completed between the 1st and the 15th of the current month. |
| Notice period (by Client) | No notice required |
| Notice period (by Subcontractor) | No notice required |

This Services Agreement is between AGS Decorating & Refurbishment Services Ltd (registered in England and Wales under number 11255408) and the subcontractor named above. The subcontractor carries on the business of painting and decorating relating to the decorating services ("the Services") specified in the Schedule above. The Client has requested the subcontractor, and the subcontractor has agreed with the Client, to provide the Services on the terms of and subject to the conditions of this agreement ("the Agreement"). It is agreed as follows:

---

## 1. Interpretation and Definitions

Unless the context otherwise requires, references to the singular include the plural and references to the masculine include the feminine, and vice versa. The headings contained in the Agreement are for convenience only and do not affect their interpretation.

A reference to a particular law is a reference to it as it is in force for the time being taking account of any amendment, extension, or re-enactment and includes any subordinate legislation for the time being in force made under it.

The Schedule forms part of this Agreement and shall have effect as if set out in full in the body of this Agreement. Any reference to this Agreement includes the Schedule.

"Client" means the person, firm or corporate body together with any subsidiary or associated company as defined by the Companies Act 2006 requiring the Services of the subcontractor and identified in the Schedule.

"Intellectual Property Rights" means patents, utility models, rights to Inventions, copyright and neighbouring and related rights, moral rights, trademarks and service marks, business names and domain names, rights in get-up and trade dress, goodwill and the right to sue for passing off or unfair competition, rights in designs, rights in computer software, database rights, rights to use, and protect the confidentiality of, confidential information (including know-how and trade secrets) and all other intellectual property rights, in each case whether registered or unregistered and including all applications and rights to apply for and be granted, renewals or extensions of, and rights to claim priority from, such rights and all similar or equivalent rights or forms of protection which subsist or will subsist now or in the future in any part of the world.

"Invention" means any invention, idea, discovery, development, improvement or innovation made by the subcontractor in connection with the provision of the Services, whether or not patentable or capable of registration, and whether or not recorded in any medium.

"Works" means all records, reports, documents, papers, drawings, designs, transparencies, photos, graphics, logos, typographical arrangements, software programs, inventions, ideas, discoveries, developments, improvements or innovations and all materials embodying them in whatever form, including but not limited to hard copy and electronic form, prepared in connection with the provision of the Services.

## 2. Substitution

The subcontractor's obligation to provide the Services shall be performed by them or a Substitute of the subcontractor as the subcontractor deems appropriate ("the Substitute"), subject to the Client being reasonably satisfied that the Substitute has the required skills, qualifications and resources to provide the Services to the required standard.

The subcontractor has the right, at its own expense, to enlist additional or substitute workers in the performance of the Services or may sub-contract all or part of the Services, provided that the subcontractor provides details, whenever requested to do so, of the additional, substitute or subcontractor ahead of the planned substitution and subject to the Client being reasonably satisfied that such additional Substitutes or any subcontractor has the required skills, qualifications, resources and personnel to provide the Services to the required standard.

Where the subcontractor provides a Substitute or sub-contracts all or part of the Services pursuant to this clause, the subcontractor shall be responsible for paying the Substitute or subcontractor and shall ensure that any agreement between the subcontractor and any such Substitute or subcontractor shall contain obligations which correspond to the obligations of the subcontractor under the terms of this Agreement, and the subcontractor shall remain responsible for the acts or omissions of any such Substitute or subcontractor.

The subcontractor shall take all reasonable steps to avoid any unplanned changes of worker assigned to the performance of the Labour Only Services, but if the subcontractor is unable for any reason to perform the Labour Only Services the subcontractor should inform the Client as soon as reasonably practicable on the first day of unavailability, and in such case shall provide a substitute subject to the provisions above.

In the event that the subcontractor is unable to supply either the original personnel or acceptable substitutes or subcontractors for a period of one week or more, then the Client is entitled to terminate this Agreement forthwith upon written notice.

The Schedule shall specify the Client, the fee payable by the Client and such disbursements as may be agreed and any other relevant information.

The Client acknowledges and accepts that the subcontractor is in business on its own account and shall be entitled to seek, apply for, accept and perform contracts to supply its services to any third party during the term of this Agreement.

## 3. The Contract

This Agreement governs the performance of the Services by the subcontractor for the Client.

The subcontractor shall not be required to provide any advice and assistance in addition to the Services and any requests to provide such additional advice and assistance shall be subject to the prior written approval of the subcontractor (at its sole discretion) and agreement between the subcontractor and the Client as to the level of fees payable for such additional advice and assistance. In the event that such additional advice and assistance is agreed, the subcontractor must notify the Client of the terms upon which such additional services will be provided, including details of any new fee arrangements, in order that the fee arrangement between the subcontractor and the Client as set out in the Schedule may be adjusted accordingly and agreed before provision of such additional services begins.

No variation or alteration of these terms shall be valid unless agreed with the Client and the subcontractor in writing, except where changes to the Services are necessary to comply with applicable Health & Safety and other statutory or regulatory requirements, in which case the subcontractor may make such necessary changes without prior notification to the Client.

## 4. Undertaking of the Subcontractor

The subcontractor warrants to the Client that by entering into and performing its obligations under this Agreement it will not thereby be in breach of any obligation which it owes to any third party.

The subcontractor warrants to the Client that its Substitutes have the necessary skills and qualifications to perform the Services. The cost for any training needed in order to gain such qualifications and skills shall be at the subcontractor's or Substitutes' own expense.

## 5. Subcontractor's Obligations

The subcontractor agrees on its own part and on behalf of its Substitutes to comply with any statutory rules or regulations including but not limited to those relating to health and safety, together with such procedures of the Client as the Client notifies the subcontractor and/or its Substitutes that it is essential that they comply with in order to properly perform the Services (including, for example, where the Services are to be performed at the premises of the Client, the health and safety policy and security arrangements) during the performance of the Services. Subject to the rules and regulations which the Client notifies the subcontractor and/or its Substitutes that it is essential to comply with, the subcontractor and/or its Substitutes shall not otherwise be bound by the policies and procedures which an employee of the Client would be bound by.

The subcontractor shall furnish the Client with any progress report as may be requested from time to time.

## 6. Circumvention and Non-Compete

Undercutting — not to submit any quotation, proposal, or offer for services to any client or potential client of the Company (the "Client") that is lower than the quote previously provided by the Company to that same Client, where such pricing information or business opportunity became known to the subcontractor through their relationship with the Company.

Client Solicitation — not to approach, solicit, or accept business from any of the Company's current or former clients (defined as any party for whom the Company has provided services in the preceding 24 months) with the intent to offer services that compete with the Company, without the prior written consent of the Company.

## 7. Equipment

The subcontractor shall provide, at its own cost, all such necessary equipment and tools as is required for the satisfactory performance by the subcontractor and any Substitutes and/or subcontractors of the Services.

If, as a matter of convenience, the subcontractor is provided with equipment and/or tools by the Client for the purpose of carrying out the Services, the subcontractor shall be responsible for preserving the security and condition of such equipment. If and to the extent that any equipment and/or tools are lost while in the subcontractor's possession, the subcontractor shall be responsible for the cost of any repairs or replacement.

## 8. Method of Performing Services

The subcontractor and its Substitutes are skilled workers who will use their own initiative as to the manner in which the Services are delivered, provided that in doing so the subcontractor shall co-operate with the Client and comply with all reasonable and lawful requests of the Client.

The subcontractor may provide the Services at such time and on such days as the subcontractor shall decide, but shall ensure that the Services are provided at such times as necessary for the proper performance of the Services.

The relationship between the parties is between independent companies acting at arm's length, and nothing contained in this Agreement shall be construed as constituting or establishing any partnership, joint venture, or relationship of employer and employee between the parties or their personnel.

Where the proper performance of the Services is dependent on the completion of tasks or services by third parties (including employees of the Client but excluding any Substitute or subcontractor of the subcontractor), the subcontractor shall have no liability to the Client for any delay, non-performance or partial performance of the Services arising from the delay or non-performance or partial performance of such tasks by third parties.

## 9. Invoicing

In line with the Construction Industry Scheme (CIS), the subcontractor is not obliged to raise an invoice on completion of works to the Client.

The Client will raise a pay statement to the subcontractor in accordance with the CIS within the agreed time as stipulated in the Schedule.

## 10. Fees

The Client will pay the subcontractor monies owed for work completed, at the frequency and for the periods of work set out in the Schedule.

The Client shall be responsible, in accordance with the Construction Industry Scheme (CIS), to deduct from the total amount the percentage of monies that falls in line with UK Government requirements.

All payments will be made to the subcontractor by a method which gives immediately available funds.

The subcontractor shall be responsible for any PAYE Income Tax, National Insurance and Pension Contributions and any other taxes and deductions payable in respect of its Substitutes or subcontractors in respect of the Services.

If the subcontractor is unable to provide the Services to the Client, no fee shall be payable by the Client during any period that the Services are not provided.

## 11. Obligations of the Client

Throughout the term of this Agreement, the Client shall pay the subcontractor in accordance with clause 10 above.

The Client shall furnish the subcontractor with sufficient information about the Services in order for the subcontractor to arrange for the Services to be carried out.

The Client will advise the subcontractor of any health and safety information or advice which may affect the subcontractor, their Substitute and/or their subcontractor, during the performance of the Services.

## 12. Term of the Agreement

This Agreement shall commence in accordance with the Schedule and shall either (as specified in the Schedule) continue until completion or the termination date as specified in the Schedule, at which time this Agreement shall expire automatically, unless previously terminated by either party giving the required notice as set out in the Schedule.

Notwithstanding the above, the Client may at any time, with no prior notice required, instruct the subcontractor to cease work on the Services where: the subcontractor has committed any serious or persistent breach of any of its obligations under this Agreement; the subcontractor has not observed any condition of confidentiality applicable to it under this Agreement; the Services are, in the reasonable opinion of the Client, unsatisfactory; the subcontractor is in breach of any statutory obligations or of such procedures of the Client as it has been notified are essential; performance of the Services is prevented for one week or more by incapacity and the subcontractor is unable to find a replacement Substitute; or the subcontractor becomes insolvent, dissolved or subject to a winding up petition.

The above provisions shall equally apply to any party performing the subcontractor's obligations under the Substitution clause.

Upon completion or termination of the Services, the Client shall be under no obligation to offer the subcontractor further work, nor shall the subcontractor be under any obligation to accept any offer made by the Client.

## 13. Intellectual Property

The subcontractor agrees that the use of the Client's name, logo and any other property containing such information shall only be used with the Client's written consent.

## 14. Confidentiality

In order to protect the confidentiality and trade secrets of the Client, and without prejudice to every other duty to keep secret all information given to it or gained in confidence, the subcontractor agrees on its own part and on behalf of its Substitutes and subcontractors: not at any time, whether during or after the performance of the Services (unless as a necessary part of the performance of its duties), to disclose to any person or make use of any of the trade secrets or confidential information of the Client, with the exception of information already in the public domain and any use or disclosure required by law; to deliver up to the Client (as directed) on completion all documents and other materials belonging to the Client (and all copies) which are in its possession; and not at any time to make any copy, abstract, summary or precis of the whole or any part of any document or other material belonging to the Client except when required to do so in the course of its duties under this Agreement.

The subcontractor shall use reasonable endeavours to procure that the provisions of this clause shall also apply to any Substitute and/or subcontractor performing the subcontractor's obligations.

## 15. Relationship Between the Client and the Subcontractor

The subcontractor acknowledges to the Client that there is no intention on the part of the subcontractor, their Substitutes and/or subcontractors, or the Client, to create an employment relationship between any of those parties, and that the responsibility of complying with all statutory and legal requirements relating to the Substitutes and/or subcontractors (including but not limited to the payment of taxation, maternity payments and statutory sick pay) shall fall upon and be discharged wholly and exclusively by the subcontractor. In the event that any person should seek to establish any liability or obligation upon the Client on the grounds that any of its Substitutes and/or subcontractors are employees of the Client, the subcontractor shall keep the Client indemnified in respect of any such liability or obligation and any related proper and reasonable costs, expenses or other losses which the Client properly incurs as a direct result.

The Client is under no obligation to offer further contracts or services to the subcontractor, nor is the subcontractor under any obligation to accept such contracts or services if offered. The subcontractor is not obliged to make its services available except for the performance of its obligations under this Agreement. Both parties agree and intend that there be no mutuality of obligations, either during or following this Agreement, whatsoever.

## 16. Notices

All notices which are required to be given as per the Schedule shall be delivered in writing.

## 17. Liability

The Client shall be liable for proper and reasonable loss, damage or injury to the subcontractor.

The Client shall ensure the provision of adequate employer's liability insurance and public liability insurance that covers Labour Only subcontractors during the performance of the Services.

## 18. Data Protection

The Client will collect and process information relating to the subcontractor, their Substitutes and/or subcontractors in accordance with national legislation.

Both parties will comply with all applicable requirements of the Data Protection Legislation. This clause is in addition to, and does not relieve, remove or replace, a party's obligations under the Data Protection Legislation.

The parties acknowledge that for the purpose of the Data Protection Legislation, the Client is the data controller and the subcontractor is the data processor.

The Client will ensure that it has all necessary appropriate consents and notices in place to enable lawful transfer of the Personal Data to the subcontractor for the duration and purposes of this Agreement.

The subcontractor shall, in relation to any Personal Data processed in connection with the performance by the Client of its obligations under this Agreement: process that Personal Data only on the written instructions of the Client unless required by law to do otherwise; maintain appropriate technical and organisational security measures against unauthorised or unlawful processing and against accidental loss or destruction of, or damage to, Personal Data; ensure all Personal Data is kept confidential; not transfer any Personal Data outside of the European Economic Area unless the prior written consent of the Client has been obtained and appropriate safeguards are in place; assist the Client, at the Client's cost, in responding to any request from a Data Subject and in ensuring compliance with its obligations regarding security, breach notifications, impact assessments and consultations with regulators; notify the Client on becoming aware of a Personal Data breach; comply with any request of the Client to amend, transfer, return or destroy Personal Data unless required by law to retain it; and maintain complete and accurate records to demonstrate compliance with this clause.

The Client consents to the subcontractor engaging any person as a sub-processor (including any Substitute) for the processing of Personal Data, subject to notifying the Client of any intended changes and giving the Client the opportunity to object. If the Client objects and the subcontractor cannot reasonably accommodate the objection, the Client may terminate this Agreement by giving not less than 30 days' written notice.

## 19. Anti-Bribery and Anti-Corruption

The subcontractor shall: comply with all applicable laws, statutes and regulations relating to anti-bribery and anti-corruption, including but not limited to the Bribery Act 2010; comply with the Client's Anti-Bribery Policy, as updated from time to time; promptly report to the Client any request or demand for any financial or other advantage received in connection with the performance of this Agreement; and ensure that its Substitutes and subcontractors comply with this clause.

## 20. Severability

If any provision or term of this Agreement shall become or be declared illegal, invalid or unenforceable for any reason whatsoever, such term or provision shall be divisible from this Agreement and deemed deleted from it, and the remainder of the provisions shall continue in full force and effect, provided that if any such deletion substantially affects or alters the commercial basis of this Agreement, the parties shall negotiate in good faith to amend the Agreement as necessary.

## 21. Entire Agreement

This Agreement constitutes the entire agreement between the parties and supersedes and extinguishes all previous agreements, promises, assurances, warranties, representations and undertakings between them, whether written or oral, relating to its subject matter.

Each party acknowledges that in entering into this Agreement it does not rely on, and shall have no remedies in respect of, any statement, representation, assurance or warranty that is not set out in this Agreement. Nothing in this clause shall limit or exclude any liability for fraud.

## 22. Counterparts

This Agreement may be executed in any number of counterparts, each of which, when executed and delivered, shall constitute a duplicate original, but all the counterparts shall together constitute the one agreement.

## 23. Third Party Rights

Except as expressly provided elsewhere in this Agreement, a person who is not party to this Agreement shall not have any rights under the Contracts (Rights of Third Parties) Act 1999 to enforce any terms of this Agreement. This does not affect any right or remedy of a third party which exists, or is available, apart from that Act.

The rights of the parties to terminate, rescind or agree any variation, waiver or settlement under this Agreement are not subject to the consent of any other person.

## 24. Governing Law and Jurisdiction

This Agreement shall be construed in accordance with the laws of England & Wales, and all disputes, claims or proceedings between the parties relating to the validity, construction or performance of this Agreement shall be subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the Courts of England & Wales.
$ags_body$,
  $ags_notes$# Notes for the solicitor: sub-contractor agreement (painters and decorators)

This is AGS's existing sub-contractor agreement, loaded into the Eco System as a template. The 24 clauses are exactly as AGS currently uses them. Only the Schedule has changed: its values are now fields the system fills in for each sub-contractor (agreement number, date, name and address, commencement and completion dates, rate), and "Hourly Rate" is now "Rate", because the system can record a day, hourly or per-job rate. Nothing here has been reviewed by a lawyer. The points below are things I noticed on reading it; they are questions for you, not conclusions.

## Employment status and CIS (the main concern)
1. **Hourly rate with fixed pay days.** An hourly rate paid on set dates twice a month, with "pay statements", reads like wages. Please advise whether AGS should pay by price for the job, day rate or schedule of rates against applications, and whether the fixed pay dates help or hurt.
2. **Control.** Clause 8 says the sub-contractor uses their own initiative, but also must "comply with all reasonable and lawful requests of the Client". Clause 5 requires progress reports and compliance with Client procedures. Please check the balance, especially for individuals.
3. **Notice.** The Schedule says no notice is needed by either side, but clause 12 refers to "the required notice", and the Client may stop work at any time where Services are "unsatisfactory in the reasonable opinion of the Client". Please check these fit together.
4. **Restrictions (clause 6).** The undercutting and client-solicitation restrictions sit awkwardly beside clause 2 ("entitled to seek... contracts... to any third party") and the statement that the sub-contractor is in business on their own account. They also use "the Company", which is not defined (the document uses "the Client"). Please advise on enforceability and on the effect on status.
5. **Substitution (clause 2).** The right looks genuine on paper. In practice AGS's high-end clients may expect the named person to do the work. Please advise on how to keep the right real.
6. **Individuals and companies.** Clause 8 describes the parties as "independent companies", but many sub-contractors are individuals. Where a sub-contractor works through a limited company, the company, not the person, should be the party. The system currently names the individual and records which way they work; please say how the agreement should differ.
7. **CIS.** Please check clauses 9 and 10 and the pay statements meet CIS requirements, including timing and verification.

## Drafting points
8. **Undefined terms:** "Labour Only Services" (clauses 2 and 17), "Data Protection Legislation", "Personal Data", "Data Subject", and "the Company". The "Substitute" definition appears inside clause 2 rather than in clause 1.
9. **Clause 2, last paragraph** says the Schedule specifies "the fee payable... and such disbursements"; the Schedule has a rate only.
10. **Clause 18.** It makes the sub-contractor the data processor of AGS's data, which looks the wrong way round for this relationship, and refers to the European Economic Area rather than UK data protection law.
11. **Clause 17.** The Client is liable for "proper and reasonable loss, damage or injury to the subcontractor" with no limit, and says AGS will insure "Labour Only subcontractors". Please check this matches AGS's actual insurance.
12. **Term.** The expected completion date is the commencement date plus 365 days. The system does not yet send annual reconfirmation reminders; that is planned.
13. **Electronic signature.** The person signs by typing their full name, and the system keeps the signed wording, their name and the time. Please confirm this is acceptable for this agreement.

## How the system uses it
The Schedule fields fill in when the person reaches the agreement step: the agreement number is allocated when AGS creates the invite (format AGS-SC-0001, counting up), the agreement date is the day the invite was created, and the commencement date is the day of signing. The signed copy is stored permanently with the exact wording, and a later change to the template does not alter anything already signed. Mark any changes in the Word copy and the template can be updated as a new version.
